---
import CopyCommand from "../components/CopyCommand.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const description = "Install and configure Pigeon for your coding agents.";
---

<Base title="Pigeon docs — set up an artifact route" description={description} active="docs">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 pb-28 pt-36 sm:px-8 sm:pt-44">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-sky">Field manual</p>
      <h1 class="mt-5 font-display text-5xl leading-none sm:text-7xl">Set the route once.</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm leading-7 text-mist/55">
        Pigeon creates the bucket, installs the agent skill, and keeps credentials in one local
        file.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-20 grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[180px_1fr]">
      <aside class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-mist/35">
        <p>Setup / 5 minutes</p><p class="mt-3">Default expiry / 90 days</p><p class="mt-3">
          Config / ~/.pigeon
        </p>
      </aside>
      <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-16">
        <section>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-coral">01</p><h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-medium">
            Prepare Cloudflare
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-mist/55">
            Create a bootstrap API token with <strong class="text-mist"
              >Workers R2 Storage Write</strong
            >. For automatic scoped-key creation, also provide a token made from Cloudflare’s <strong
              class="text-mist">Create additional tokens</strong
            > template.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-mist/55">
            For strict separation, pass them independently as <code class="text-sky"
              >--r2-token</code
            > and <code class="text-sky">--token-token</code>. Bootstrap tokens are never stored.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-coral">02</p><h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-medium">
            Run setup
          </h2>
          <div class="mt-5">
            <CopyCommand command="npx @leomosley/pigeon init --account YOUR_ACCOUNT_ID" />
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-mist/55">
            Set <code class="text-sky">CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN</code> for bucket management and
            <code class="text-sky">CLOUDFLARE_TOKEN_TOKEN</code> for scoped-key creation. Prefer environment
            variables over shell history.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-coral">03</p><h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-medium">
            Use pre-made credentials
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-mist/55">
            Avoid API Tokens Write entirely by creating bucket-scoped R2 credentials in Cloudflare
            first.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-5">
            <CopyCommand
              command="npx @leomosley/pigeon init --account YOUR_ACCOUNT_ID --with-key"
            />
          </div>
        </section>
        <section>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-coral">04</p><h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-medium">
            Check the route
          </h2>
          <div class="mt-5"><CopyCommand command="npx @leomosley/pigeon doctor" /></div>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-mist/55">
            Doctor uploads a tiny probe, reads it over the public route, then deletes it.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section class="rounded-xl border border-white/[0.08] bg-white/[0.03] p-6">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-medium">Agent prerequisites</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-mist/55">
            Agents use <code class="text-sky">aws-cli</code> for upload. Screenshot capture uses native
            tools or headless Chromium. Pigeon installs the shared skill at <code class="text-sky"
              >~/.agents/skills/pigeon</code
            > and links Claude’s global skill directory when safe.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-medium">Lifecycle commands</h2>
          <div class="mt-5 grid gap-3 font-mono text-xs text-mist/60">
            <code>pigeon env --shell sh</code><code>pigeon rotate</code><code>pigeon destroy</code>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-mist/55">
            <code class="text-sky">rotate</code> works for Pigeon-managed keys. <code
              class="text-sky">destroy</code
            > empties and deletes the bucket before removing local config.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
